    "title": "Jerry Jones' daughter makes comments on Super Bowl controversy MAGA fans won't like - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Jeremy Goldstein ,\n5 hours ago\nDallas Cowboys owner Jerry Jones is a larger donor to the Republican Party. Many prominent GOP figures, including President Donald Trump, have come out and spoken against Bad Bunny performing at the Super Bowl halftime show.\nWhile NFL commissioner Roger Goodell has been adamant that the Puerto Rican artist is the right choice , many have still objected.\nJones has not spoken publicly about Bad Bunny. His 58-year-old daughter, Charlotte, was asked about the upcoming Super Bowl halftime show on \"The Katie Miller Podcast\" - hosted by the wife of top Trump crony Stephen Miller - and didn't mince her words.\n\"I think when you think about the Super Bowl, you want the No. 1 performer in the world to be there,\" she said. Bad Bunny is the most-streamed artist on Spotify in 2025.\n\"We're on a global stage and we can't ever forget that,\" Charlotte added. \"Our game goes out to everybody around the world and to get the premier entertainer to want to be a part of our game, I think is amazing. We have a mixed culture.\"\nBad Bunny is the most streamed artist in the world\nBad Bunny's recent tour didn't include any stops in the United States. \"There was the issue of like, -",
